  "Question": "Use the quadratic formula to solve \\(3x²+5x-1=0\\). Which result is correct?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(x=(5\\pm\\sqrt{37})/6\\)",
    "B": "\\(x=(-5\\pm\\sqrt{13})/6\\)",
    "C": "\\(x=(-5\\pm\\sqrt{37})/3\\)",
    "D": "\\(x=(-5\\pm\\sqrt{37})/6\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(a=3\\), \\(b=5\\), \\(c=-1\\), \\(b²-4ac=25+12=37\\), and \\(x=(-5\\pm\\sqrt{37})/(2\\times3)=(-5\\pm\\sqrt{37})/6\\). A omits the negative sign in \\(-b\\), B miscalculates the discriminant, and the denominator in C should be \\(2a=6\\).",
